# NeonBench release-signing key — OpenSSH allowed_signers format.
#
# Use this to verify the detached signature over a release's SHA256SUMS:
#
#   ssh-keygen -Y verify -f docs/allowed_signers \
#     -I louvetvicente@gmail.com -n file \
#     -s SHA256SUMS.sig < SHA256SUMS
#
# The key is hardware-backed (FIDO2 / YubiKey Security Key NFC): the private
# half never leaves the authenticator and every signature needs a physical
# touch. That is what the signature attests — "the key holder vouched for these
# bytes" — and nothing more. It does NOT make the binaries code-signed, so
# Windows SmartScreen still warns. See the README's "Downloads and trust".
#
# fingerprint: SHA256:BwjB7xoV0U94xza5wGG9ZfLPgDl+hDpLKv9A5HVKgvQ
#
# `scripts/sign-release.sh --check` asserts the fingerprint above still matches
# the key below, so this comment cannot silently drift.

